          "number": 2,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "For most scientists, the answer is no. So much so that, according to experts in neuroscience(神经系统科学), our brains do not handle multitasking situations well. As soon as two tasks require our attention, productivity suffers. What we call multitasking, therefore, is in reality the ability to move more or less quickly from one task to another. This requires two essential conditions: that one of the tasks needs to be automatic, like walking or eating, and that they both need different mental processes. Answering the phone and writing at the same time, for example.",
          "chinese": "对于大多数科学家来说,答案是否定的。以至于根据神经系统科学专家的说法,我们的大脑无法很好地处理多任务情况。一旦两项任务需要我们的注意力,生产力就会下降。因此,我们所说的多任务处理,实际上是或多或少快速地从一项任务转换到另一项任务的能力。这需要两个基本条件:其中一项任务需要是自动的,比如走路或吃饭,并且两项任务都需要不同的心理过程。例如,同时接电话和写作。",
